Module 1: Networking Fundamentals



1. Computer Network
Definition
A Computer Network is a collection of two or more devices connected together to share data, resources, and services.

Why do we need a Network?

Share files
Share printers
Internet access
Communication (Email, WhatsApp, Video Calls)
Resource sharing
Real-Life Example

Your laptop and mobile are connected to the same Wi-Fi and can share files.

Key Points
Connects multiple devices.
Can be wired or wireless.
Uses protocols for communication.

⭐ Interview Answer
A computer network is a group of interconnected devices that communicate and share data and resources using communication protocols.

