2. Types of Computer Networks


****PAN (Personal Area Network)
Definition

A network covering a very small area around one person.

Range

Up to 10 meters

Examples
Bluetooth Earbuds
Smartwatch
Wireless Keyboard



*****LAN (Local Area Network)
Definition

A network covering a small area like a home, office, or school.

Examples
College Lab
Office Network
Home Wi-Fi
Advantages
High speed
Low cost

*****MAN (Metropolitan Area Network)
Definition

A network covering a city.

Example

City-wide cable TV network.

*****WAN (Wide Area Network)
Definition

A network covering countries or the entire world.

Example

Internet

Memory Trick
PAN → Personal

LAN → Local

MAN → Metropolitan (City)

WAN → Worldwide
⭐ Interview Answer

PAN connects personal devices, LAN connects devices within a small area, MAN covers a city, and WAN connects devices over very large distances. The Internet is the best example of a WAN.

