7. Client-Server Architecture
Definition
In Client-Server Architecture,

Client sends a request.
Server processes the request.
Server sends the response.
Real-Life Example
Open YouTube

↓

Browser sends request

↓

YouTube Server

↓

Server sends video

↓

You watch the video
Examples

Client

Chrome
Mobile App
Laptop

Server

Google Server
Netflix Server
Amazon Server
Key Points
Client requests services.
Server provides services.
Most websites use this architecture.
⭐ Interview Answer

In Client-Server Architecture, the client requests a service, and the server processes the request and returns the response.

Interview Questions
What is Client-Server Architecture?
Give a real-life example.
