8. Peer-to-Peer (P2P)
Definition

In Peer-to-Peer Architecture, every computer can act as both a client and a server.

There is no central server.

Example

Torrent File Sharing

Key Points
No central server.
Direct communication.
Suitable for small networks.
⭐ Interview Answer

In Peer-to-Peer Architecture, all computers communicate directly with each other without a central server.

Interview Questions
What is Peer-to-Peer Architecture?
Give one example of P2P.
9. Client-Server vs Peer-to-Peer
Client-Server	Peer-to-Peer
Central server	No central server
More secure	Less secure
Easy to manage	Hard to manage
Used by websites	Used for file sharing
