1. What is Data Communication?
Definition

Data Communication is the process of transferring data between two or more devices through a communication medium.
Simple Example

You send "Hi" to your friend on WhatsApp.

Your phone ➜ Internet ➜ Friend's phone

This is data communication.

Why do we need it?

Without data communication:

❌ No WhatsApp
❌ No Email
❌ No YouTube
❌ No Google
Key Points
Transfers data between devices.
Uses communication protocols.
Can be wired or wireless.
⭐ Interview Answer

Data communication is the process of exchanging data between two or more devices using a communication medium and communication protocols.

Interview Questions
What is Data Communication?
Give a real-life example of Data Communication.


2. Components of Data Communication
There are 5 basic components.

Sender → Medium → Receiver
       ↘ Protocol ↙
      Message


***A. Sender
Definition
The device that sends the data.

Example
Laptop
Mobile
Computer


B. Receiver
Definition
The device that receives the data.

Example

Your friend's phone.

C. Message
Definition
The information being sent.

Example
Text
Image
Video
Audio
Document


D. Transmission Medium
Definition
The path through which data travels.

Types
Wired
Ethernet Cable
Optical Fiber

Wireless
Wi-Fi
Bluetooth
Mobile Network

E. Protocol
Definition
A protocol is a set of rules that devices follow while communicating.
Without protocols, devices cannot understand each other.

Examples
HTTP
HTTPS
TCP
UDP
FTP
Easy Example
Imagine two people speaking.

If one speaks English and the other speaks Japanese, they won't understand each other.

Similarly, computers need common rules (protocols) to communicate.

⭐ Interview Answer

The five components of data communication are Sender, Receiver, Message, Transmission Medium, and Protocol.

